course: dictionary
lesson: 6381
title: Mulch: a garden word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special topic, such as gardening. «Leafcutter ants chew leaves into a mulch to grow a fungus garden.» The words around mulch give clues: the ants chew leaves, and they use the result to grow something. So a mulch is plant material, chewed or cut up, that helps things grow.
explain: Gardeners also use mulch. A mulch is a layer of material such as bark, leaves, straw or compost spread on soil around plants. Ask yourself what the layer does. It keeps the soil moist, and it keeps weeds down, so it helps the plants more than it hurts them.
explain: Mulch can also be a verb. To mulch means to spread mulch on the soil. «We mulched the flower beds» means we covered the soil around the flowers with a layer of bark. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: «We spread a layer of bark on the flower beds» still makes sense.
fact: Mulch is a layer of material such as bark, leaves, straw or compost spread on soil around plants.
fact: Mulch keeps soil moist and keeps weeds down.
fact: As mulch rots, it adds nutrients to the soil, which helps plants grow.
fact: To mulch means to spread mulch on soil.
fact: «Leafcutter ants chew leaves into a mulch to grow a fungus garden.»
exercise: «Leafcutter ants chew leaves into a mulch to grow a fungus garden.» What is mulch? | A hard, shiny stone | A sort of bird | *Plant material chewed up or cut up to help things grow | A wet, sticky sweet
exercise: In a school garden, the children spread bark mulch around the roses. Why do gardeners use mulch? | *To keep the soil moist and keep weeds down | To make the soil dry out faster | To stop plants from ever growing | To make the soil freeze solid
exercise: «The gardener will mulch the beds on Monday.» What does mulch mean here? | To water the plants with a hose | *To spread mulch on the soil | To dig a hole for a tree | To pick the flowers
test: The bark mulch keeps the soil moist and keeps weeds ___. | *down | happy | up | loud
test: Yesterday we ___ the flower beds with bark. | mulcher | mulchy | mulches | *mulched
exam: Which best describes mulch? | A tool for cutting grass | *A layer of bark, leaves, straw or compost spread on soil around plants | A kind of plant with bright flowers | A type of insect
